WEBVTT

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:08.440
Interstellar travel was once a one-way trip,
with no possibility of returning.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.690
After immeasurable sacrifice,
humanity miraculously

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:15.950
found a planet with water
within the habitable zone

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.240
of a spectral class-G star.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.620
This planet, named "Sea of the Morningstar,"

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:25.830
received extensive funding
as one of the earliest colonized planets.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.840
And now...

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.800
Kurihara, wait!

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.260
Hey, wait!

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.240
What did you do?

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.400
Weren't you watching?

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.740
I fired a signal round.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.370
Don't worry.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.370
The cartridge was old,

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.040
so it doesn't have the power
of a normal flash round.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.080
Why did you do that?

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:30.920
Let's go.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.670
I want to talk to you,
somewhere farther away.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:45.260
Kidnapping?!

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.980
I don't know their affiliation,
but surely you could tell

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.020
that they were intent on grabbing you, right?

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.730
Who knows where they'd have taken you,

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.980
had you been stupid enough to follow.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.650
Why would they do that?

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.030
Don't you get it?

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.990
It's because you're Kato Marika.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:05.700
By the way, your customers were likely

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.410
military intelligence,

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.620
a police task force,

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:10.500
Stellar Military Special Ops...

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:10.870
De

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:11.250
li

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:11.620
cious

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.920
And perhaps even some space
mafia enforcer squads?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.380
That would-be kidnapper is probably getting
beat up by them as we speak.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.300
It's his own fault, though.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.140
What were all those people doing there?

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.310
It's because...

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.270
It's because they were all
sent to watch you.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.520
Because you might become the next captain of the Bentenmaru.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:34.860
Kurihara, do you...

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.530
Thank you for the dessert.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.650
You appear to have a lot of questions.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.110
Of course I do!

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.490
But aren't there already
people you could ask?

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:49.330
Your ride is here.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.750
Lamp House

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.250
Is everyone at the Lamp House okay?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.800
Don't worry.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.300
They're all fine.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.840
Marika is all right.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:03.760
That's great!

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.890
Tell everyone I'll be right back!

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.770
We know you're safe now,
so you can go home.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:11.390
No.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.270
I left my stuff there, and I haven't changed.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:16.230
And...

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:17.570
It was delicious.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.650
I have one customer to ring up.
It was delicious.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.360
Closed Temporarily

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.990
Goodbye!

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.760
Ririka...

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.850
Don't you have work?

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.890
If you say your daughter's been caught in the middle of a gunfight,

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:56.520
usually, they'll let you go home early.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.690
It must've been tough.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:03.990
I'd planned to tell you
when you graduated.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:05.910
Are you mad?

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.410
About what?

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.700
About the pirates...

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.030
About being captain...

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.200
And about your dad.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.830
I'm more surprised.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.540
About the pirates, sure...

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.590
But also to find out that Dad was alive,

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:22.170
and only died recently.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.380
I'm sorry.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.720
No, it isn't like that.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.760
The stuff about my dad
just doesn't feel real.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:32.850
I'm surprised at myself
for not feeling anything.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:35.600
I see.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.610
Ririka...

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.240
You were a pirate too,

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.120
weren't you?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.950
So, you did your homework, huh?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.750
That's right.
I was on the Bentenmaru.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.250
Why were you a pirate?

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.170
I was born in space.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.760
The first thing I knew was
being on a spaceship.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:05.720
That's all.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.050
But that's...

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:12.510
It's probably impossible
for you to imagine.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.060
But people like that do exist.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.810
They're people who found their place in space.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.560
They're sailors...

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.990
Let's go on a little trip.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.200
We'll drop off the bike at home, and then head out.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.990
I'd like to get some things together too.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.860
What is all this?

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.320
Can't you tell?

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.440
Guns.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:10.490
But why do you have these?

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.200
The police will arrest you.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.160
They're for self-defense.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.120
The police and the military let it slide.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.830
That's some pretty big stuff they're letting slide...

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:28.170
This might be good for our first fireworks.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.510
Put these on.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:35.850
Or it'll blind you.

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:44.360
I'm gonna fire it.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.580
It's been a long time...

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.670
The recoil is like a cannon.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.130
I love it.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:08.300
Wanna try?

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:14.510
I wouldn't start you off with something so huge.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:15.760
You'd start with something smaller.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.720
Actually, this one's plenty big...

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.850
The ArmaLite Armor-Penetrating Beam Gun.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:23.850
I remember this one...

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.490
They used to give it to me for work.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.360
Yeah, just like that.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.450
Hold it like that, and the
recoil won't affect you.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.040
Okay.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:46.330
Do you know why pirates boarding other ships take guns?

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.210
To fight?

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:50.880
No,

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.010
to impress.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.180
To impress?

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:55.130
That's right.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.430
Ninety percent of the time,

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:00.260
a fight is decided before
the first trigger is pulled.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:03.810
However, if you set a gun to full power and pull the trigger,

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.640
someone will die, or...

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.020
it might be you who dies.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.400
In the police or the military,

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:14.450
so long as you follow orders, you don't need to worry about such things.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:15.860
However,

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.870
pirates must decide for themselves
whether to pull the trigger.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:23.080
That is the power of a pirate.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.120
The power of a pirate...

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:53.150
What you hold in your hands

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.110
is power.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:58.660
If you become captain of a pirate ship,

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.990
you'll have to pull the trigger
of an even greater power.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:06.790
But I still haven't decided
what I'm going to do!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.960
You don't have to decide right now.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.670
You already have the heart

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:15.380
and the resolve required to decide.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.760
This power is yours alone.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.970
My power...

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.150
Space Yacht Club

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:38.860
I'm Kane McDougal,
your new club advisor.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.030
Hello, everyone.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.970
So, you're going on a practice cruise?

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.100
Yeah.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:08.140
You could just see their eyes
sparkle when I told them

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.980
that I have a large ship license.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.060
Oh?

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:17.030
We're going to do an on-board
check over the long weekend.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:19.400
We'll leave after the closing ceremonies.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:22.450
So that's why Hyakume sent over this data, huh?

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:24.370
Yeah, I asked him to.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.910
Analyzing
It's huge, so I was wondering about it.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.870
Hakuho Academy Senior High School

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:29.210
Let's see...

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.170
A solar sailor?

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.380
Two hundred years old?

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.670
It was an experimental craft at first.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:40.340
Then it was a transport.
Then an exploratory vessel...

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.800
And during the war of independence...

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:43.890
Ambush of Enemy Convoy Successful

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:44.430
It was an armed merchant vessel,
and a camouflaged cruiser?!

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.930
Ship Hakuchou
Armed Merchant

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:49.060
One of the ancient pirate ships

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.890
known as the Original Seven, the Hakuchou.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:52.940
Seriously?

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.060
A girls' school has a pirate ship?

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.290
Ah...

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.580
So this is the Odette II?

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:12.370
Yes,

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:14.670
the yacht club's practice ship.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.250
And this hanger...

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.300
This is a completely different scale.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.420
It's just for this ship's use.

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:23.800
There's nothing else they can do with it,

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.430
so it's supposedly quite inexpensive.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.720
On the surface, anyway...

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:28.600
Sorry?

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.310
Oh, nothing.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:36.190
Welcome Aboard

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.280
Okay, the hatch is open.

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:42.650
Thanks.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:45.320
Let's go, Captain.

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:47.030
Aw, cut that out.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.700
I'll inspect the exterior before I board.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.500
A pre-flight check, right?

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.460
Naturally.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.790
Everyone, get inside first.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:00.130
Begin the inspection of your assigned area.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:00.960
Right!

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.890
That's some thick armor.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:10.100
And on a girls' school practice ship to boot.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.440
The hull looks fine.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.150
How about the inside?

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:30.620
Hurry, hurry!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:31.490
Roger!

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:33.290
Huh?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:35.960
Hurry, hurry!

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.580
Hurry!

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.040
Hey...

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.090
Advisor!

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:44.420
I've finished checking the life support circulation systems.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:47.550
The Mess hall's refrigeration systems are functioning properly.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.220
Roger!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.510
Keep at your inspections.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:52.350
Yes, sir.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:54.680
This is zero gravity...

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:55.390
Calm down!

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:58.020
Yes, sir!

00:13:58.020 --> 00:13:59.560
Is she a kid?

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.020
I guess she is just a kid.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.230
Now, then...

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:05.360
The bridge, huh?

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:06.780
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.040
Hey, now...

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.840
How's it going?

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.380
What are you thinking?

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:27.010
Me?

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.590
What do you mean?

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:29.930
Becoming our advisor,

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.050
and taking us on this practice cruise.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.930
What are you planning?

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:38.640
Your upperclassmen were the
ones who suggested the cruise.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.440
It's all just a coincidence.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:44.150
It was coincidence that I
joined the yacht club,

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.150
and coincidence that you were there.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:47.690
What a coincidence...

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:50.910
Really, I'm lucky.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:53.990
Okay, everyone.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:58.160
The central computer update is complete.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:01.830
I'm cutting all power to the bridge and rebooting.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.500
Has everyone finished?

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:05.800
I'm done.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:07.010
Finished.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:08.510
See, right there...

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:11.050
We're good!

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:12.430
I'm ready too.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:15.850
Bridge to C68, port-side.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.020
Can you hear me?

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:18.310
This is port-side.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:19.520
We hear you.

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:22.270
We're rebooting the main bridge.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:24.650
Bridge-side, final inspection!

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:34.370
Cutting pier-side external power in three seconds.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:35.740
Three...

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:36.790
Two...

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:37.790
One.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.120
External power, cut.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.330
Did it shut down?

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:43.960
Cut confirmed.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:46.800
Reconnect the power when
I count down from ten.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:47.630
Okay.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:48.710
Ten...

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:49.630
Nine...

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:50.760
Eight...

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:51.630
Seven...

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:52.630
Six...

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:53.640
Five...

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:54.640
Four...

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:55.680
Three...

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:56.640
Two...

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:57.640
One...

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:59.080
Zero.

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:09.070
My, my...

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:12.700
Do you always boot up
your ships this way?

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.070
Not at all.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:16.160
We've been doing it stand-alone until today,

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:18.040
because we were still
using the old system.

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:21.830
We're doing it a bit rougher than usual,

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.460
since we're updating navigation.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:26.170
A bit rougher, huh?

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:27.090
Advisor!

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:29.550
Someone is here to see you.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:31.380
Bye.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:39.470
So, how is your student, faculty advisor?

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.940
She's a good student. I'm impressed.

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:46.310
And her piloting skills aren't bad, either.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:50.400
Must be pretty good,
for you to say that.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:51.820
Yeah.

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:55.910
But being a captain
isn't about piloting skill.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.660
That's true.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.990
But if she's a good pilot,
she can anticipate

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:02.370
the ship's movement, as well as
adjust for the atmosphere.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.080
That's a good thing.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:05.250
I guess so.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.750
And she'll be sailing one
of the survivors of

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:10.420
the legendary Original Seven,
just like our Bentenmaru.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:13.470
I'm looking forward to our practice cruise.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.230
Geez...

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:27.020
What is that pirate teacher thinking?

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:28.310
About the duty roster?

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.730
Does it matter?

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:34.740
It isn't at all unusual for first years to be grouped together.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:37.700
Or perhaps...

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.240
Maybe he's trying to figure out

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:42.830
my motives by pairing you with me?

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:48.080
Um, thanks.

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:50.460
For what?

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:54.010
Earlier. I never said thanks.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:55.340
Thanks for saving me.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:57.800
I didn't save you.

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.470
I simply couldn't bear to watch.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.430
They call that saving—

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:02.470
No, they don't!

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:08.810
Hey...

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:10.610
What are you doing?

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.900
A lot of people are

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:15.400
trying to break in from the outside.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:20.030
This ship isn't stand-alone.
It's connected to the network now.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:22.780
So, of course, it's being
attacked externally.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.290
The Odette II is under electronic attack?

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:28.920
That is what I'm saying, yes.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:30.040
From where?

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:32.130
Who'd go after a girls' school practice ship?

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:34.710
It isn't worth making a big deal over.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.420
At the moment,

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:39.590
it's merely auto-patrolling robots and spam viruses.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:43.350
Oh, just typical cyber-attacks then.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:44.770
I just hope it stays that way.

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:50.310
I feel like someone else
is making an attempt.

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:53.230
The basic idea of electronic warfare

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:55.440
is to take over the enemy's
system before they notice.

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:57.570
So that's what you were up to.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:58.530
Do you know who it is?

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.240
I can't tell right now,

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:04.330
unfortunately.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.000
What?

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.290
I think I'll try my hand

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:10.370
at electronic warfare!

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:10.870
Wai—

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:14.920
I went forward too far...

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.050
Do you even know how to use that?

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:18.010
Nope.

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:24.220
It's reacting to something.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.520
I thought so.

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.890
It's synchronized to the
external communication.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.060
External?

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.270
The ship's antenna?

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:36.110
The long-range main antenna is folded up...

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:38.820
So it's from the short-range external antenna?

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:41.360
It isn't sensitive enough to do
anything while we're docked.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.530
A direct cable!

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.410
The electronic attacks
aren't coming from outside.

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:50.290
They're from inside the relay station!

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.960
That appears to be correct.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:54.670
Okay...

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:58.840
We'll narrow down the
comm system filters

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.470
to the direct lines we're wired into.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.300
Found you!

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:09.310
The ships that are docked here...

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.560
The D-block docking port.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.400
The infiltration protocol

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:17.270
is being posted from the
D-block docking port.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:18.150
Wait a second...

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:20.150
There are fifteen ships

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:21.360
at that port.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:21.900
Roger.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.620
Port 117...

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:33.790
Port 117.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:36.460
The Lightning 11 is docked at Port 117!

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:38.090
It docked four days ago...

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:39.960
No scheduled launch date.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:43.090
Too obvious.

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:45.340
Why would a simple transport

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:48.510
have a large antenna like that unfolded?

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:54.980
Let's give this electronic warfare a try.

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:58.440
Do you know what electronic warfare is?

00:20:58.440 --> 00:20:59.320
Nope.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:03.400
Only computers equipped for
cyber-warfare can boot up.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.910
They're attacking via cable, right?

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:07.620
So we should fight too.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:09.080
Are you insane?

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:12.000
A total amateur can't
engage in electronic warfare.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.660
Let's pull the comm cable.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:17.420
Tomorrow, we can explain the
situation to Kane-sensei...

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:18.540
That won't work!

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:19.710
It'll be too late!

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:22.510
If you lose in electronic warfare,

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.220
you lose control of your ship, right?

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:27.300
Even I understand that much!

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:29.850
If they're trying to do
something that awful,

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:31.680
we have to counterattack.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:34.060
We must teach them a lesson,

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:35.940
or they'll just do it again.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:38.400
So...

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.150
Don't blame me for what happens.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:43.900
Just so we're clear,

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:46.490
I don't know much about
electronic warfare, either...

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.370
You're pretty decisive.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:52.830
I wasn't expecting that.

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:54.500
It's something I'm good at!

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:01.460
Make the best decision you can.

00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:03.880
And believe in it!

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.260
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.390
My Power, the Power of a Pirate

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:12.470
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:17.980
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:20.980
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:24.360
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.450
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:30.490
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:39.420
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.300
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:48.130
How far?

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.800
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:54.430
Until the end.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:55.770
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:59.100
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:07.940
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:11.700
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:13.120
What should we do?

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.290
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:20.580
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:26.630
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:30.880
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:41.480
Her first electronic battle.

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:43.060
Her first practice cruise.

00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:47.360
The tides of fate pull the girl toward the great sea.

00:23:48.280 --> 00:23:50.450
What will the sparkle of space

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:52.570
that she sees tell her?

00:23:53.820 --> 00:23:55.830
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:55.830 --> 00:23:57.580
The Odette II leaves port.

00:23:57.580 --> 00:23:58.950
Look forward to it.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:04.960
The Odette II Leaves Port!

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:10.210
Make the best decision you can!
